  "description": "A thin, async-only client for the Gmail REST API and the Google OAuth 2.0 token endpoints, with no dependency on Google.Apis. List, read and send messages (via messages.send, so the single gmail.modify scope is enough), incremental sync with history.list, labels, trash, attachments, plus authorization URL building, code exchange, token refresh and revocation. You supply an access-token provider; the library never stores tokens. Every non-2xx response becomes a GmailApiException with the Google error reason and flags for expired history, revoked authorization and rate limiting; 429 / 5xx are retried with exponential backoff. No third-party MIME library: outgoing mail is composed by a built-in RFC 822 writer (GmailOutgoingMessage) or supplied as raw RFC 822 bytes. Targets netstandard2.0, netstandard2.1, net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0.",
